<title>CHINA: China's 1997 edible oil buying detailed.</title>
<headline>China's 1997 edible oil buying detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table shows the three edible oil import figures of five major Chinese customs offices as well as the country of origin in 1997.</p>
<p>Details were provided by the General Administration of Customs of China.</p>
<p>Figures are in tonnes. Percentages represent the share of the total market. Percentages may not add up to 100 percent because details of some smaller import regions and supplying countries have not been included.</p>
<p>------SOYOIL</p>
<p>    May imports  64,103   Jan-May total imports   495,016</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	     May	  Pct	   Jan-May	 Pct</p>
<p>    Shanghai	 5,018	 7.8	   49,079	  9.9</p>
<p>    Huangpu	    500	 0.8	   36,318	  7.3</p>
<p>    Tianjin		0	 0.0	   90,199	 18.2</p>
<p>    Nanjing	  9,500	14.8	   68,501	 13.8</p>
<p>    Jiulong	 14,954	23.3	   76,815	 15.5</p>
<p>(Shenzhen)</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Brazil	  25,543	39.8	   22,431	 45.3</p>
<p>    Argentina     12,951	20.2	   55,946	 11.3</p>
<p>    U.S.	    19,999	31.2	  190,776	 38.5</p>
<p>    Malaysia	 5,551	 8.7	   19,749	  4.0</p>
<p>------PALM OIL</p>
<p>    May imports   90,867   Jan-May total imports    344,050</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	     May	  Pct	   Jan-May	 Pct</p>
<p>    Jiulong	 10,923	12.0	   71,033	 20.6</p>
<p>(Shenzhen)</p>
<p>    Shantou	   3479	 3.8	   26,691	  7.8</p>
<p>    Nanning	   2388	 2.6	   19,416	  5.6</p>
<p>    Huangpu	  6,345	 6.9	   30,216	  8.7</p>
<p>    Zhanjiang     11,490	12.6	   38,612	 11.2</p>
<p>ORIGINS</p>
<p>    Malaysia	68,289	75.1	   255,489	74.2</p>
<p>    Indonesia	2,009	22.1	    75,446	21.9</p>
<p>------RAPESEED OIL</p>
<p>    May imports   27,053   Jan-May total imports    131,835</p>
<p>  CUSTOMS	     May	  Pct	   Jan-May	 Pct</p>
<p>    Jiulong	 21,940	81.1	   98,396	 74.6</p>
<p>(Shenzhen)</p>
<p>    Zhanjiang	    0	 0.0	    4,054	  3.1</p>
